WEBVTT

00:04.400 --> 00:09.280
<i>It hasn't even been a month since 
I came to this new world, Etelldia,</i>

00:09.630 --> 00:11.990
<i>but I've gotten used to life here.</i>

00:12.500 --> 00:16.450
<i>Alan and Elena were nervous around 
unfamiliar people at first,</i>

00:16.880 --> 00:18.780
<i>but they've gotten used to it now, too.</i>

00:20.610 --> 00:22.870
<i>Our party, White Wings,</i>

00:23.160 --> 00:25.750
<i>works on quests for two 
days, then takes a day off.</i>

00:26.710 --> 00:29.300
<i>That's the cycle we've been 
keeping up as adventurers.</i>

00:34.230 --> 00:38.720
It's good, but I feel like 
it's missing something...

00:38.720 --> 00:39.830
Huh?

00:39.830 --> 00:41.180
Why?

00:42.100 --> 00:47.150
This world has three types of bread: 
white, rye, and whole grain.

00:47.850 --> 00:50.230
They're all very simple, 
which is fine, but...

00:50.560 --> 00:54.610
I kinda miss my fancy dressed-up 
breads and dessert breads.

00:54.610 --> 00:55.510
Desert breads?

00:55.510 --> 00:56.770
Dress-up breads?

00:59.970 --> 01:02.910
I know! We'll just make some ourselves!

01:02.910 --> 01:04.520
I'll make some!

01:04.520 --> 01:05.840
I'll make some!

01:05.840 --> 01:07.110
Desert bread!

01:07.690 --> 01:09.210
Dress-up bread!

01:09.460 --> 01:10.620
Desert bread!

01:10.620 --> 01:11.840
Dress-up bread!

01:21.310 --> 01:27.600
<b>A Journey Through Another World: 
Raising Kids While Adventuring</b>

02:43.010 --> 02:46.470
<b>The Golden Bakery</b>

02:43.510 --> 02:48.520
<b>Nice to Meet You, Joule</b>

02:47.620 --> 02:48.930
Hello.

02:48.930 --> 02:51.770
Welcome! What can I get for you?

02:52.180 --> 02:55.200
Actually, I'm not here to buy.

02:55.200 --> 02:57.210
I wanted to ask you a favor.

02:57.210 --> 02:58.040
Huh?

02:58.040 --> 02:59.610
What's up, Michelle?

02:59.920 --> 03:03.460
This customer seems to have a 
favor he wants to ask of us.

03:03.460 --> 03:04.330
A favor?

03:04.670 --> 03:06.720
Oh, this is my father, Rhode.

03:06.720 --> 03:07.540
Welcome.

03:07.830 --> 03:09.600
My name is Takumi.

03:09.600 --> 03:12.140
I was hoping you could 
make some bread for me...

03:14.940 --> 03:16.320
using these.

03:17.390 --> 03:18.530
Jam?

03:19.150 --> 03:21.340
And I don't know what this yellow stuff is.

03:21.660 --> 03:23.840
It's called custard cream.

03:23.840 --> 03:26.560
I'd like you to put these inside 
the bread before baking it.

03:26.560 --> 03:29.020
What? Put them inside the bread?

03:29.020 --> 03:31.350
Right. Or is that impossible?

03:31.350 --> 03:35.440
It's not impossible, but I've 
never made anything like that.

03:38.170 --> 03:40.860
In that case, I'll show you how to do it.

03:55.460 --> 03:56.590
I get it!

03:56.860 --> 03:58.800
Let's see... So we do this...

03:59.120 --> 03:59.840
Like this?

03:59.840 --> 04:01.510
Yeah! I can see you're a pro!

04:01.920 --> 04:04.470
Okay, let's try this "custard" stuff, too.

04:04.470 --> 04:06.690
Michelle, help me out.

04:06.690 --> 04:07.260
Okay!

04:07.630 --> 04:08.540
Me, too!

04:08.610 --> 04:09.470
Me, too!

04:09.470 --> 04:12.790
Ah, you little ones want to help us?

04:12.790 --> 04:13.810
Yes!

04:13.810 --> 04:15.440
Good answer!

04:15.440 --> 04:16.370
Yes!

04:16.370 --> 04:17.790
You're helping, too.

04:17.790 --> 04:18.770
S-Sure!

04:19.210 --> 04:20.660
Okay, then...

04:21.740 --> 04:24.530
Anko

04:21.740 --> 04:24.530
<b>Red beans boiled</b>

04:21.740 --> 04:24.530
<b>until sweet</b>

04:22.000 --> 04:24.530
Let's put this anko in some of them, too.

04:58.620 --> 05:00.940
Okay, they're done!

05:04.400 --> 05:06.090
This is delicious!

05:06.090 --> 05:09.620
It really is! I had no idea they'd 
be so good with things baked inside!

05:12.320 --> 05:14.850
Don't eat too fast. 
It'll get stuck in your throat.

05:15.720 --> 05:16.790
Takumi.

05:17.590 --> 05:20.020
Do you mind if we sell these at the store?

05:20.020 --> 05:22.310
Under your name, of course. 
And we'll pay you—

05:22.310 --> 05:23.260
No, no.

05:23.570 --> 05:26.590
Just being able to buy them from 
now on will be enough for me.

05:26.590 --> 05:28.800
I just wanted to eat some of these.

05:28.140 --> 05:33.470
<b>Cream</b>

05:28.140 --> 05:33.470
<b>Bread</b>

05:28.140 --> 05:33.470
<b>Strawberry</b>

05:28.140 --> 05:33.470
<b>Jam</b>

05:28.140 --> 05:33.470
<b>Red Bean</b>

05:28.140 --> 05:33.470
<b>Bun</b>

05:28.800 --> 05:31.480
<i>They're sold all over the 
place in my old world,</i>

05:31.480 --> 05:33.470
<i>so it wasn't even my idea.</i>

05:33.900 --> 05:36.030
Boy, I sure appreciate this!

05:36.030 --> 05:39.470
Michelle, let's experiment 
with some other fillings!

05:39.470 --> 05:39.940
Sure!

05:40.680 --> 05:43.400
Alan, Elena, did you like those?

05:43.690 --> 05:45.360
Yummy!

05:45.650 --> 05:47.240
We want more!

05:47.240 --> 05:48.320
More?!

05:51.280 --> 05:54.240
<b>The Next Day</b>

05:54.630 --> 05:57.830
Congratulations! 
You've been promoted to rank E!

06:00.040 --> 06:05.630
<b>Status</b>

06:00.040 --> 06:05.630
<b>Name: Takumi Kayano 
Race: Human? Disciple of the god of wind (temp.) 
Job: — 
Age: 20 
Level: 13 
Skills: Light magic 50, Dark magic 50, Wind magic 150, 
Time-space magic 100, Daily-use magic 100, 
Swordsmanship 50, Throw 18, Appraise 200, Dismantle 100, 
Cooking 85, Sewing 23, Washing 12, Cleaning 31, 
Craftsmanship 37, Arithmetic 107, Reading 125, 
Status resistance 300, Mental resistance 300, 
Physical attack resistance 300, Magic attack resistance 300 
Titles: Other-worldly reincarnation 
One who has received the blessing of the creator Marianolla 
Friend of the wind god Sylphyryll</b>

06:00.040 --> 06:05.630
m 0 0 l 270 0 l 270 170 l 0 170

06:00.680 --> 06:03.240
Oh, I'm level 13 now.

06:03.240 --> 06:05.630
You moved up especially fast for a Newcomer!

06:05.630 --> 06:07.370
Really?

06:07.370 --> 06:09.990
<i>I guess it's good if I can 
do a wider range of jobs now.</i>

06:10.960 --> 06:13.850
Alan and Elena here worked 
hard, too. Didn't you?

06:20.670 --> 06:22.400
By the way, Takumi...

06:22.710 --> 06:24.980
Are you interested in going to the labyrinth?

06:24.980 --> 06:27.110
Labyrinth? Oh...

06:27.510 --> 06:30.060
<i>According to the knowledge 
Syl instilled in me,</i>

06:30.060 --> 06:33.330
<i>there are 108 labyrinths in this world.</i>

06:33.630 --> 06:38.160
There's a labyrinth near Shireen 
that has 15 underground floors.

06:38.480 --> 06:41.330
Not many truly dangerous monsters 
show up around the city,

06:41.330 --> 06:45.200
so many adventurers visit the labyrinth 
once they get used to them.

06:45.200 --> 06:46.130
Huh...

06:46.420 --> 06:48.620
Then maybe we'll go there next, huh?

06:48.620 --> 06:50.040
Let's go! Let's go!

06:50.040 --> 06:51.470
What? Right now?!

06:51.780 --> 06:55.670
I did say it's close, but it still 
takes half a day to walk there,

06:55.670 --> 06:58.990
and it would probably take a 
few days to fully conquer it...

06:58.990 --> 07:00.160
Ah, no.

07:00.160 --> 07:03.020
I thought we'd check out the first
couple of floors just to get a feel for it.

07:03.490 --> 07:05.340
Ah, of course!

07:05.340 --> 07:08.990
It just seems like you three would 
keep going deeper and deeper.

07:09.370 --> 07:13.320
Oh, please. You expect too 
much of an E-rank adventurer.

07:19.120 --> 07:20.720
<i>Despite what I said...</i>

07:21.940 --> 07:25.130
<i>We've already gone down 
as far as the third floor.</i>

07:25.680 --> 07:29.800
<i>Or more like Alan and Elena are 
taking us through it so accurately</i>

07:26.430 --> 07:27.550
This way!

07:28.430 --> 07:29.800
That way!

07:29.800 --> 07:31.970
<i>that we didn't get lost at all.</i>

07:29.800 --> 07:32.510
That way! This way! That way!

07:32.510 --> 07:36.220
<i>And the two of them always point 
in the same direction, somehow.</i>

07:35.150 --> 07:36.220
That way!

07:36.550 --> 07:39.140
<i>Twins sure work in mysterious ways.</i>

07:36.550 --> 07:39.140
This way! That way! This way!

07:43.000 --> 07:45.690
<i>So this is called the Earth Labyrinth, huh?</i>

07:45.960 --> 07:48.590
<i>And all the monsters in it are earth-type.</i>

07:52.440 --> 07:53.550
Monster!

07:53.550 --> 07:55.820
Oh, that's a Ground Mole.

07:56.220 --> 07:59.300
They're weak, so you two should 
be able to defeat it alone,

07:59.300 --> 08:00.790
but still, be caref—

08:00.790 --> 08:02.110
We beat it!

08:02.110 --> 08:02.750
That was fast!

08:05.420 --> 08:06.210
Huh?

08:07.090 --> 08:08.010
The mole...

08:08.010 --> 08:09.170
...disappeared.

08:09.430 --> 08:13.460
Monsters in labyrinths disappear 
when defeated, apparently.

08:13.460 --> 08:14.490
Weird, huh?

08:14.490 --> 08:15.640
Weird.

08:15.940 --> 08:19.280
But they usually drop items in their place.

08:19.280 --> 08:23.810
And some of their drops can 
be really valuable or rare.

08:23.810 --> 08:25.600
Drops?

08:25.870 --> 08:28.690
Drops, drops...

08:29.140 --> 08:30.200
Found it!

08:30.920 --> 08:33.620
This... must be a Mole whisker.

08:33.620 --> 08:35.370
Doesn't look like it's worth much...

08:35.370 --> 08:36.640
Not worth much!

08:36.700 --> 08:37.820
Not worth much!

08:51.250 --> 08:54.130
Okay, I think that's enough for today.

08:55.390 --> 08:57.220
Why don't we have dinner?

08:59.100 --> 09:01.510
With this magical cookstove device,

09:01.510 --> 09:04.060
we can have a hot meal 
no matter where we are.

09:05.060 --> 09:07.520
Guineafowl and 
Vegetable Soup

09:30.380 --> 09:31.630
<b>The Next Day</b>

09:31.750 --> 09:33.260
Wind Cutter!

09:41.390 --> 09:44.560
<i>After that, we continued to kill monsters,</i>

09:44.560 --> 09:46.520
<i>eat dinner,</i>

09:46.520 --> 09:48.480
<i>sleep, and then repeat that loop for a while.</i>

09:48.780 --> 09:52.940
<i>After a few days, we'd made 
it down to the tenth floor.</i>

10:02.720 --> 10:03.890
What's that?

10:03.890 --> 10:05.540
It's a treasure chest.

10:05.840 --> 10:09.000
What's inside might be really cool,

10:09.000 --> 10:10.890
or it might be something dangerous.

10:10.890 --> 10:12.270
Can we open it?

10:12.270 --> 10:13.250
Hang on a sec.

10:16.750 --> 10:19.090
Looks like it's not a trap. You can open it.

10:19.090 --> 10:20.640
Let's open it!

10:25.010 --> 10:26.520
Two potions, huh?

10:26.520 --> 10:29.900
Stamina Potion

10:26.520 --> 10:29.900
Restores stamina 
when consumed

10:26.990 --> 10:29.900
A stamina potion that restores 
your stamina when you drink it,

10:29.900 --> 10:32.860
Mana Potion

10:29.900 --> 10:32.860
Restores magic power 
when consumed

10:30.380 --> 10:32.860
and a mana potion that restores your magic.

10:32.860 --> 10:36.440
They're low-ranked items, 
so there's not much in them.

10:36.800 --> 10:38.130
Taku!

10:48.400 --> 10:51.460
Thanks, you guys. You saved me.

10:51.900 --> 10:53.670
It's a Wild Ape hide.

10:54.310 --> 10:55.360
Is it rare?

10:55.360 --> 10:56.760
Somewhat, maybe.

10:56.760 --> 10:57.750
Somewhat!

10:57.750 --> 10:58.780
Maybe!

11:00.250 --> 11:01.250
Somewhat!

11:01.250 --> 11:02.380
Maybe!

11:02.380 --> 11:03.380
Somewhat!

11:03.380 --> 11:04.620
Maybe!

11:05.620 --> 11:09.140
<i>Their perception and martial 
arts sense are really something.</i>

11:09.810 --> 11:11.780
<i>They just keep moving with no hesitation,</i>

11:11.780 --> 11:14.020
<i>they find monsters so quickly...</i>

11:14.470 --> 11:18.860
<i>It must come from instinct rather 
than calculation or training.</i>

11:19.110 --> 11:20.290
Somewhat!

11:19.110 --> 11:23.160
<i>I'm really glad they weren't picked 
up by someone in a position of power.</i>

11:20.290 --> 11:21.280
Maybe!

11:21.280 --> 11:22.260
Somewhat!

11:22.260 --> 11:23.160
Maybe!

11:23.530 --> 11:26.990
<i>Maybe that's what Syl was so worried about.</i>

11:26.990 --> 11:30.760
<i>It does feel a lot like I'm 
just using them, though...</i>

11:30.760 --> 11:31.820
It's coming!

11:34.540 --> 11:36.340
Clay Snake

11:35.190 --> 11:37.000
A Clay Snake?

11:37.000 --> 11:39.920
That one has venom in its fangs. 
You guys stay back, okay?

11:39.920 --> 11:41.170
Okay!

11:43.440 --> 11:45.640
<i>This might be the time to try my Throw skill.</i>

11:49.180 --> 11:50.640
Wind Cutter!

11:54.280 --> 11:56.030
Taku, there's more!

11:56.030 --> 11:57.360
A bunch of them flying!

11:58.030 --> 11:59.820
Those are Giant Bees.

11:59.820 --> 12:01.440
We'll beat 'em!

12:01.440 --> 12:05.010
They don't have venom, 
but still, be careful of their stingers.

12:05.010 --> 12:05.910
Okay!

12:15.040 --> 12:16.170
Huh?

12:17.610 --> 12:21.340
<i>Oh... So they can use Throw, too...</i>

12:21.670 --> 12:23.010
Over there!

12:23.990 --> 12:25.850
That way!

12:25.850 --> 12:26.870
Over there!

12:26.870 --> 12:28.640
<i>Are they having trouble for once?</i>

12:27.640 --> 12:28.640
Over there!

12:29.160 --> 12:31.730
<i>I'll help if it looks like 
they're in danger, but...</i>

12:33.810 --> 12:35.240
That way!

12:35.240 --> 12:36.400
Over there!

12:37.520 --> 12:40.360
<i>They're obviously just playing a game of tag.</i>

12:40.850 --> 12:43.200
<i>While they're keeping the 
monsters busy with their game,</i>

12:41.110 --> 12:43.200
Inventory

12:43.680 --> 12:46.030
<i>maybe I'll sort the drops we've picked up.</i>

12:48.070 --> 12:52.330
<i>Ground Spider's web, Wild 
Ape fang, Slime jelly...</i>

12:52.970 --> 12:55.110
<i>I wonder if I could use this for something.</i>

12:55.110 --> 12:57.670
<i>It feels really nice and cool...</i>

13:02.900 --> 13:04.510
<i>Oh, they killed one.</i>

13:15.110 --> 13:16.730
We beat 'em!

13:16.990 --> 13:18.980
Yeah! You did great.

13:19.410 --> 13:21.060
Dropped items!

13:22.070 --> 13:25.410
Hey, this... is honey!

13:25.410 --> 13:28.410
Honey is a pretty precious 
commodity in Etelldia.

13:28.780 --> 13:29.720
Way to go!

13:29.800 --> 13:30.870
Way to go!

13:31.100 --> 13:36.750
Alan, Elena, let's take out all 
the Giant Bees we see from now on!

13:36.750 --> 13:37.710
Okay!

13:38.510 --> 13:40.420
Oh, there's some already!

13:40.800 --> 13:42.480
We'll beat 'em!

13:46.480 --> 13:47.560
Just hang on.

13:48.010 --> 13:51.220
I'm gonna make something really tasty.

13:51.220 --> 13:52.170
Me, too!

13:52.240 --> 13:53.300
Me, too!

13:53.300 --> 13:54.180
We'll help!

13:56.540 --> 13:58.050
Then we take this...

13:58.880 --> 14:00.740
Soak it well, and...

14:01.230 --> 14:02.220
fry it!

14:04.000 --> 14:08.060
Then we add plenty of the honey 
we just collected, and...

14:08.700 --> 14:11.280
There you go! The French toast is done!

14:11.770 --> 14:13.370
Let's eat!

14:16.480 --> 14:18.040
Yummy!

14:22.410 --> 14:24.240
Pretty good, if I do say so myself.

14:25.510 --> 14:27.970
Oh, our prey is back again.

14:28.560 --> 14:30.830
I'll get this one. You guys keep eating.

14:34.240 --> 14:35.600
Air Shot!

14:40.000 --> 14:40.850
Again?

14:41.190 --> 14:42.770
Wind Cutter!

14:43.820 --> 14:44.860
Taku!

14:44.860 --> 14:45.780
There's more!

14:46.130 --> 14:49.490
They must be attracted to 
the scent of the honey.

14:49.490 --> 14:50.760
Honey!

14:50.760 --> 14:51.700
We'll get some!

14:54.660 --> 14:56.620
Hon... Hon...

14:56.620 --> 14:57.880
<i>Instant kill...</i>

14:56.620 --> 14:58.620
...ney! ...ney!

14:58.620 --> 15:02.290
We can get all the honey we want out of this!

15:02.860 --> 15:06.830
<i>So, while still gathering a 
ton of honey along the way,</i>

15:06.830 --> 15:09.860
<i>we finally arrived at the lowest
 floor, the fifteenth floor.</i>

15:12.050 --> 15:15.110
I bet that's the door to 
the final boss's room.

15:15.110 --> 15:16.930
It just has that look.

15:16.930 --> 15:18.020
Final boss?

15:25.840 --> 15:27.570
This room's huge.

15:32.050 --> 15:32.900
Huh?

15:32.900 --> 15:33.870
It closed.

15:39.200 --> 15:42.640
A giant earthworm? So this is the final boss?

15:42.640 --> 15:46.920
I get it. So we can't get out of 
here until we beat this guy, huh?

15:47.440 --> 15:50.900
Alan, Elena, let me handle this one.

15:50.900 --> 15:52.620
You two wait here, okay?

15:54.310 --> 15:56.880
Now, we'll start with a little trial run.

15:57.700 --> 15:58.900
Wind Cutter!

16:02.020 --> 16:04.360
It's surprisingly fast for something so huge!

16:09.030 --> 16:10.150
<i>Sand Ball?</i>

16:10.440 --> 16:13.150
<i>It knows magic, too? Definitely a final boss.</i>

16:13.150 --> 16:14.350
Air Shot!

16:15.240 --> 16:16.830
Wind Arrow!

16:23.360 --> 16:25.640
That ended quicker than I expected.

16:25.640 --> 16:28.640
But is that because it was the 
final boss of a low-rank labyrinth,

16:28.640 --> 16:32.260
or because the powers Syl 
gave me are overpowered?

16:32.260 --> 16:33.590
Leave it to me!

16:33.590 --> 16:36.260
A fang and... is this a fairy stone?

16:36.260 --> 16:38.300
And there's Worm meat...

16:38.300 --> 16:40.330
This is apparently a coveted ingredient,

16:40.330 --> 16:43.440
but I don't think I'd want 
to eat earthworm meat...

16:45.510 --> 16:46.720
All done?

16:46.720 --> 16:47.480
The end?

16:47.480 --> 16:49.840
Thanks for waiting. We're all done.

16:49.840 --> 16:51.840
You guys aren't hurt, are you?

16:51.840 --> 16:53.290
We're fine!

16:54.000 --> 16:54.560
Hey...

16:54.560 --> 16:55.600
...Taku!

16:55.600 --> 16:56.160
Yeah?

17:03.440 --> 17:06.080
Were you praising me because I worked hard?

17:10.710 --> 17:12.990
I see! Well, thanks!

17:20.060 --> 17:22.720
This must be one of those 
teleportation devices that

17:22.720 --> 17:24.500
instantly sends us back to the top floor.

17:25.310 --> 17:26.350
Taku!

17:26.600 --> 17:28.040
Treasure chest!

17:31.400 --> 17:35.110
<b>[Fire Bomb]</b>

17:31.400 --> 17:35.110
A bomb that 
explodes 
after the 
one who 
imbued it 
with magic is 
a certain distance away

17:33.090 --> 17:35.110
Fire Bombs...

17:35.650 --> 17:37.500
<i>"A bomb that explodes after</i>

17:37.500 --> 17:41.280
<i>the one who imbued it with magic
is a certain distance away," huh?</i>

17:41.280 --> 17:43.830
<i>So it's something like a grenade?</i>

17:43.830 --> 17:44.790
Yay!

17:44.840 --> 17:45.580
Yay!

17:45.580 --> 17:46.290
Hey!

17:47.330 --> 17:49.680
These are dangerous,
so I'll put them away, okay?

17:49.680 --> 17:50.710
Okay!

17:51.390 --> 17:54.800
Okay, Alan, Elena, touch that crystal ball.

18:10.120 --> 18:11.570
We're outside!

18:11.570 --> 18:12.840
Outside!

18:12.840 --> 18:14.980
It's been so long since we saw the sun!

18:16.010 --> 18:18.080
Well, ready to head back to town?

18:18.080 --> 18:19.170
Taku...

18:20.080 --> 18:21.070
Doggy!

18:21.070 --> 18:21.780
Huh?

18:22.180 --> 18:25.250
<i>No, that's... a wolf!</i>

18:26.550 --> 18:29.750
<i>Is it a regular animal or a monster?</i>

18:34.340 --> 18:37.480
<i>It acts a lot like a pet dog...</i>

18:37.480 --> 18:40.040
<i>Alan and Elena don't seem 
concerned about it at all.</i>

18:40.040 --> 18:41.510
<i>Maybe it's not dangerous?</i>

18:42.150 --> 18:43.010
Appraise.

18:43.010 --> 18:48.230
<b>Status</b>

18:43.010 --> 18:48.230
<b>Race:\h\hFenrir</b>

18:43.010 --> 18:48.230
<b>[Takumi's 
contracted beast]</b>

18:43.010 --> 18:48.230
<b>Age: 5</b>

18:43.010 --> 18:48.230
<b>Level: 25</b>

18:43.010 --> 18:48.230
<b>Skills: Water magic, Ice magic, Claw Slash, 
Regenerate, Shrink, Night Vision, Perception</b>

18:45.110 --> 18:46.580
<i>Yep, it's a monster.</i>

18:46.580 --> 18:48.230
<i>And an S-ranked one!</i>

18:48.470 --> 18:51.230
<i>And... "Takumi's contracted beast"?</i>

18:51.230 --> 18:53.790
<i>I don't remember signing any contract...</i>

18:55.170 --> 18:56.650
<i>I bet Syl's behind this.</i>

19:02.760 --> 19:05.500
Um... You're a contracted beast?

19:09.110 --> 19:10.080
Paw.

19:10.790 --> 19:11.790
Down.

19:12.070 --> 19:12.910
Sit.

19:14.470 --> 19:17.660
<i>That expectant look in its eyes... Is it...</i>

19:26.480 --> 19:27.220
What's up?

19:28.030 --> 19:29.440
Wait, are you...

19:30.050 --> 19:30.690
Paw?

19:31.040 --> 19:32.240
Woof!

19:32.240 --> 19:34.150
<i>Imitating a Fenrir?!</i>

19:34.150 --> 19:37.360
Okay, I get it! Paw! Paw!

19:38.550 --> 19:39.880
So fluffy!

19:39.880 --> 19:41.120
And cute!

19:41.120 --> 19:41.930
I'm Alan!

19:41.930 --> 19:43.000
I'm Elena!

19:43.950 --> 19:45.130
Taku.

19:45.800 --> 19:46.780
A name.

19:46.780 --> 19:48.210
He needs one.

19:48.210 --> 19:51.750
Huh? Oh, right... Let's see...

19:52.460 --> 19:54.460
How about Joule?

19:55.510 --> 19:56.630
Joule!

19:56.760 --> 19:57.880
Joule!

19:57.880 --> 19:59.420
Nice to meet you!

20:01.120 --> 20:04.110
We can't take Joule with us any farther.

20:04.110 --> 20:05.260
Aw...

20:05.260 --> 20:06.260
Why not?

20:06.780 --> 20:10.710
Well, everyone would be scared if they 
saw a monster walking around town.

20:11.220 --> 20:15.180
So, Joule, I'll have you hide 
in my shadow for the time being.

20:18.160 --> 20:19.170
Joule...

20:19.170 --> 20:20.550
...disappeared!

20:20.550 --> 20:21.530
Don't worry.

20:21.880 --> 20:25.360
The use of contracted beasts 
is a type of dark magic.

20:25.360 --> 20:27.610
They normally stand by 
within the user's shadow,

20:27.610 --> 20:30.430
and they can be summoned 
into the open when needed.

20:32.650 --> 20:33.960
Syl, you there?

20:33.960 --> 20:38.670
Takumi! You didn't come back 
for so long! I missed you!

20:39.540 --> 20:41.340
Sorry to get right to business,

20:41.340 --> 20:43.760
but I have some questions 
about the contracted beast.

20:43.760 --> 20:44.880
Contracted beast?

20:45.190 --> 20:46.910
You know, the Fenrir monster.

20:46.910 --> 20:48.220
You sent him, didn't you?

20:48.560 --> 20:50.850
Hey! The Water... No fair!

20:50.850 --> 20:53.440
I wanted to send you one first!

20:53.440 --> 20:55.030
You mean it wasn't you?

20:55.030 --> 20:57.180
I'll send you one soon, too!

20:57.180 --> 20:59.470
Tomorrow morning, in the 
grassland outside town...

20:59.470 --> 21:00.780
H-Hang on!

21:01.230 --> 21:03.900
You said "Water." Did you 
mean the God of Water?

21:05.020 --> 21:08.080
More specifically, the head of 
the God of Water's household.

21:08.080 --> 21:09.740
I guess they wanted to thank you.

21:10.200 --> 21:12.520
I have lots of other things from them, too.

21:10.840 --> 21:12.520
<i>Thank me?</i>

21:12.520 --> 21:14.310
<i>For taking in Alan and Elena?</i>

21:12.520 --> 21:14.310
I'll send them to you now.

21:16.740 --> 21:19.220
<i>Their skills all come from water magic,</i>

21:19.220 --> 21:23.830
<i>so I did think if they were involved with 
any god, it'd be the God of Water...</i>

21:27.260 --> 21:36.140
Inventory

21:28.260 --> 21:31.120
Is it really okay for me to accept all this?

21:31.120 --> 21:33.150
Yes, please do!

21:33.760 --> 21:36.010
They said they'd send more later, too.

21:36.010 --> 21:38.810
What? No, I get the idea already, really...

21:38.810 --> 21:41.730
Expect divine punishment 
if you don't accept them.

21:41.730 --> 21:42.860
This is a god, after all.

21:43.260 --> 21:45.820
<i>Is he threatening me?</i>

21:49.820 --> 21:53.780
<i>Exhausted by our several days 
spent conquering the labyrinth,</i>

21:53.780 --> 21:58.150
<i>we returned to the inn and fell 
asleep the moment we hit the bed.</i>

21:58.150 --> 21:59.480
<i>H-Heavy...</i>

21:59.480 --> 22:03.570
<i>Then, the next morning, I headed out 
to the grassland Syl mentioned...</i>

23:45.020 --> 23:50.030
<b>Next Time</b>

23:45.520 --> 23:50.030
<b>Monster Hunting!</b>

23:46.080 --> 23:47.290
Monster...

23:47.290 --> 23:49.010
...Hunting!
